erif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=150 valign=top style='width:112.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Adult<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=36 valign=top style='width:27.05pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>:<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=111 valign=top style='width:83.35pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>0.0\r\n  - 200.0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>NOTE:-<\/span><\/b><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'> <\/span><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Allergic\r\nreactions, which are becoming more widespread, are usually diagnosed on the\r\nbasis of medical history and clinical symptoms. In vitro and in vivo testing,\r\nhowever, play a key role in confirming clinical suspicions and tailoring\r\ntreatment. The measurement of immunoglobulin E (IgE) in serum is widely used in\r\nthe diagnosis of allergic reactions and parasitic infections. Many allergies\r\nare caused by the immunoglobulins of \u00a0subclass IgE acting as point of contact\r\nbetween the allergen and specialized cells. The IgE molecules (MW 200,000) bind\r\nthe to the surface of mast cells and basophillic granulocytes. Subsequently the\r\nbinding of allergen to cell \u2013bound IgE causes these cells to release histamines\r\nand other vasoactive substances. The release of histamines in the body results\r\ninitiates what is commonly known as an allergic reaction.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Before making any\r\ntherapeutic determination it is important, however, to know whether the\r\nallergic reaction is IgE mediated or non-IgE mediated. Measurement of total IgE\r\nin serum sample, along with other supporting diagnostic information, can help\r\nto make that determination. Measurement of total circulating IgE may also be of\r\nvalue in the early detection of allergy in infants and as a means of predicting\r\nfuture atopic manifestations. Before deciding on any therapy it is important to\r\ntake into consideration all the relevant clinical information as well as\r\ninformation supplied by specific allergy testing.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>IgE levels show a\r\nslow increased during childhood, reaching adult levels in the second decade of\r\nlife. In general, the total IgE levels increased with the allergies a person\r\nhas and the number of times of exposure to the relevant allergens. Significant\r\nelevations may be seen on the sensitized individuals, but also in cases of\r\nmyeloma, pulmonary aspergillosis, and during the active stages of parasitic\r\ninfections.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Clinical correlation is suggested. <\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DRAWN\r\nSAMPLE FROM OUTSIDE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>LisaScan-EM (Semi-Automated Clinical Chemistry\r\nAnalyzer)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US>.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span style='position:relative;z-index:251657728;left:-52px;\r\ntop:469px;width:994px;height:471px'><i